<p>The problem here is that <code>Base::foo</code> is a dependent (on template parameter) name and conforming C++ implementation must issue an error at <code>foo();</code> invocation. The difference between <code>/std:c++17</code> and <code>/std:c++20</code> is that the latter implies <code>/permissive-</code> which (among other things) disables legacy name lookup in favor of more stand-conforming behavior.</p>
<p>In order to fix this error you need to write <code>Base&lt;T&gt;::foo();</code>.</p>
